`out.state` beside `out.journal`. `L-4` makes `state.md` a projection
of the journal and says the journal wins when they disagree, so the
committed copy was a second source of truth the rule itself calls
non-authoritative — rewritten after every outcome, and a guaranteed
conflict between any two batch branches. `perp state` renders it back
byte for byte, which is what makes leaving it out safe. Verified by
hashing both.

Nothing tested that it was being staged, which is how it stayed that
way; there is a test now.

