The failing test exposes a real bug in my fix: `self.touched` is a *deduplicated* list of paths (by design, for `G-3` staging and the step-level "did anything change" check). A model that writes the same file three times — exactly the "careful, re-verifying" case `L-11`'s test covers — only grows `touched` on the *first* write. Using `touched.len()` growth as the per-turn signal makes every repeat write to an already-touched path look quiet, which is wrong: the workspace did change, again.

The honest per-turn measure isn't "did the deduplicated set grow" but "did a call this turn actually execute a workspace-mutating tool successfully" — determined from the real result, not guessed pre-execution from the tool name (which was `is_progress`'s bug), and not gated by whether that exact path had been touched before in this step (which is a staging concern, not a progress one). I'll have `run_calls` report that per-turn fact directly.

